{"4503170": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "XYLOMETAZOLINE", "steam_appid": 4503170, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4503170/extras/e40c1aac9166008e20c2693266d873f7.poster.avif?t=1778941512\" width=1170 height=146 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4503170/extras/e40c1aac9166008e20c2693266d873f7.webm?t=1778941512\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4503170/extras/e40c1aac9166008e20c2693266d873f7.mp4?t=1778941512\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>XYLOMETAZOLINE</strong> is a surreal, first-person narrative experience rooted in the PSX-horror aesthetic. It explores the harrowing struggle of addictions that regulate both the physical and emotional state, portrayed through a dependency on nasal drops. It is a philosophical journey through a world where every living being is hooked on something, and the line between substance and habit has blurred into an existential nightmare.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You are nobody. When a mysterious car accident leaves a package for a stranger's &quot;daughter&quot; in your hands, you are thrust into a journey through brutalist estates, the abandoned offices of the XYLOLIFE corporation, and liminal spaces.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4503170/extras/4e47550dfb595f63d3d9bd2c73ca589e.poster.avif?t=1778941512\" width=1170 height=146 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4503170/extras/4e47550dfb595f63d3d9bd2c73ca589e.webm?t=1778941512\" 